Test 7 failed — spaces-only input. When all chars in a row are spaces, rstrip removes them all, leaving an empty string. But the spec says "all characters from the input should also be present in the transposed output" and spaces are characters. The issue is: we only rstrip trailing spaces, but when a whole row is spaces, they all get stripped.

The key insight: we should only strip trailing spaces from columns that extend beyond the last non-space character in that column. Let me think about this differently.

The rule is: "pad to the left with spaces, don't pad to the right." This means each output row should have exactly enough columns to cover the input rows that have content at that column position, but no extra trailing spaces.

Let me reconsider: for each output row (which corresponds to an input column), the length should be determined by how many input rows have a character at that column index. Rows shorter than that index get a space, but we shouldn't add trailing spaces beyond the last row that has content.
